>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (I am Aarya S. Burande, and I recently completed my first year of B.Tech in IT Engineering at VJTI. My interests lean towards AI architectures and modelling, I really enjoy figuring out how different models work. The satisfaction of finally unravelling a puzzle and optimizing it to solve a real-world problem is immensely rewarding. Moreover, the chance to actually design those puzzles is unparalleled.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (Currently, I mostly work with C++ and Python, and I enjoy exploring different fields whenever I get the chance. While researching for this project, I stumbled across several topics that I found incredibly fascinating. I often had to stop myself from disappearing down rabbit holes just to stay focused on the project itself. That said, those rabbit holes are exactly what made the experience exciting, and I would love to learn more about those areas in the future.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (I picked this project specifically because it brought together several topics that I was curious about, such as AI architectures, graph models, and drug interactions. The more I read about it, the more questions I had. To be honest, it seemed really cool, and I wanted to be a part of the group working on it. I was very interested in DNA interactions and protein structures back in 10th grade, so in a way, this project reconnected me with an older curiosity while introducing me to entirely new ideas.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
