224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (Both representations provide different information. SMILES tells us what the drug is chemically, while the graph tells us how the drug interacts biologically. Since drug interactions depend on both chemical structure and biological context, combining these representations may provide a more complete understanding of drug-drug interactions than either approach alone.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
